{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia","id":1443001,"title":"Malkavians and heterochromia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-07T12:01:16-07:00","id":1443001,"title":"Malkavians and heterochromia","content":"How do you think, did malkavian female protagonist have heterochromia before her Embrace or this is consequence of malkavian blood, or even impact of her sire?<br /> Interestingly, heterochromia seems to be common among malkavian females. Jeanette also has heterochromia (Therese, however, hasn't), as well as Malkavian character from VTM Swansong - <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/kMSS0xt.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/kMSS0xt.png</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","user":"trueann","date":". 04-07-2021, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T12:16:37-07:00","id":1443004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trueann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia#post1443001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you tihk, did malkavian female protagonist have heterochromia before her Embrace or this is consequence of malkavian blood, or even impact of her sire?<br /> Interestingly, heterochromia seems to be common among malkavian females. Jeanette also has heterochromia (Therese, however, hasn't), as well as Malkavian character from VTM Swansong - <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/kMSS0xt.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/kMSS0xt.png</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a nice visual striking image for characters who are one thing and another. Though in the case of canon, I'd just take the boring answer that the eyes helped attract their sires.<br /> <br /> Another one is that they're using Obfuscate subtlety.<br /> <br /> But anything is possible in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T12:21:02-07:00","id":1443005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia?p=1443004#post1443004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another one is that they're using Obfuscate subtlety.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or contacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T13:44:36-07:00","id":1443017,"title":"","content":"My No Prize answer for heterochromia appearing in Malkavian Kindred would either be 1.) it\u2019s a manifestation of their inherent connections to the Malkavian Cobweb (the most likely in my opinion) or 2.) the appearance of heterochromia is carried in Jacob/Esau\u2019s \u201cbloodline\u201d (much less likely, but still possible as the Protagonist is at least 8th Generation, we know Jacob/Esau are involved in Jeanette and Therese\u2019s Embrace, and we don\u2019t know a lot of information about Leysha yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T01:24:38-07:00","id":1443097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trueann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia#post1443001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think, did malkavian female protagonist have heterochromia before her Embrace or this is consequence of malkavian blood, or even impact of her sire?<br /> Interestingly, heterochromia seems to be common among malkavian females. Jeanette also has heterochromia (Therese, however, hasn't), as well as Malkavian character from VTM Swansong - <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/kMSS0xt.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/kMSS0xt.png</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jeanette does not have heterochromia.<br /> <img src=\"http://img10.reactor.cc/pics/comment/Vampire-the-Masquerade-Bloodlines-%D0%98%D0%B3%D1%80%D1%8B-Jeanette-Voerman-ero-cosplay-3386288.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T01:52:07-07:00","id":1443100,"title":"","content":"ehm, left eye is azure, and the right one is green...so I'd say...yes she has heterochromia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T08:14:14-07:00","id":1443123,"title":"","content":"Teresse does not. It's contacts or obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know about goths because I'm young and sweet, but I don't think i'm stepping to far outa line to say malks and goths probably overlap slightly more than goths and other clans (maybe Toreador compete?). an odd contact isn't entirely uncommon among goths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-08-2021, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T09:25:06-07:00","id":1443128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia?p=1443123#post1443123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teresse does not. It's contacts or obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a reason it couldn\u2019t just be naturally occurring heterochromia that has nothing to do with being a vampire? Like CTPhipps said, it may have been a trait that appealed to her sire","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T10:49:39-07:00","id":1443140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia?p=1443123#post1443123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teresse does not. It's contacts or obfuscate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you so sure? It is possible that<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> color just chages when Jeanette is in control. It is malkavian blood, after all.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T12:52:33-07:00","id":1443156,"title":"","content":"Mental illness does not cause funky eyes. Magic in WoD generally follows the path of least resistance; fancy light shows don't appear everytime you cast a spell, you just cast a spell. With this in mind, why would a magical malkavian weakness, which effects purely the mind, have physical characteristics to tell everyone somethings happening? Side-effects like paradadox and formori ugliness are side-effects for useful, possitive powers that go against nature, while the Malkavian weakness is itself a negative item that isn't going to manifest an additional negative item to balance it out. Especially since vampires generally are physically static creatures that, outside of the ups and downs of paths, the paleness of age, and a few other outliers generally resist appearance changes that occur after the first week or so of being embraced. Heterochromia isn't a fucking novelty malkavian trick, and as a clan that specializes in obfuscate and auspex and is filled with people hiding debilitating mental illnesses, it's unfitting for them to have a physical marker that to advertise that they're the crazy ones and they're so crazy that sometimes their eye colour changes. The more I think of it, the more I positively loath the idea. (It could be a Maeghar mark, but strange stigmas are literally the defined weakness of Maeghar, because their whole deal is that everyone sees them as 'other'. Go play Maeghar if you really want to push this idea. A Tremere with an Arcane curse might also work)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T10:48:26-07:00","id":1443378,"title":"","content":"Just found out about <i>Lord Theron - </i>Malkavian from GC-2, whose eyes are described as bicolored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T08:51:16-07:00","id":1443600,"title":"","content":"And maybe the explanation is simple: Malkavians are at least weird. And they are attracted to weirdness. Heterochromia isn't a norm in human population so it can be seen as weirdness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T09:20:28-07:00","id":1443602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia?p=1443156#post1443156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mental illness does not cause funky eyes. Magic in WoD generally follows the path of least resistance; fancy light shows don't appear everytime you cast a spell, you just cast a spell. With this in mind, why would a magical malkavian weakness, which effects purely the mind, have physical characteristics to tell everyone somethings happening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically it is because eyes are windows to the soul and the instability inflicted by Malkav's blood is a terrible burden that warps that inner self.<br /> <br /> I do not think it needs an explanation beyond it being one of the many ineffable gifts of the First Seer's blood.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> Any theorizing that Malkavian heterochromia is physiological overlooks the great pink elephant in the room. Malkavians spread madness like butter. The heterochromia is an unconscious Dementation effect that Jeanette inflicts on those who look at her.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T10:17:55-07:00","id":1443611,"title":"","content":"Thats a pretty poor use of Dementation. Why would you develop a power thats not good for anything, especially when Obfuscate 3 exists and its in-clan for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T10:56:09-07:00","id":1443614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia?p=1443611#post1443611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats a pretty poor use of Dementation. Why would you develop a power thats not good for anything, especially when Obfuscate 3 exists and its in-clan for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could not be developed. It could be unconsious, uncontrolable effect, just as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> wrote. Some kind of &quot;bonus&quot; from a ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T12:07:37-07:00","id":1443625,"title":"","content":"Ah so like you're playing mage and suffering from paradox... rather than vampire. <br /> <br /> There's a few ways to get Heterochromia post embrace; Vicissitude, Chimestry, Arcane curse, Infernal pacts. Any of these are far more interesting and less obnoxious than ' I got this eye when I became a member of The Crazy Bloodline'. Imagine how that might feel to someone with any of the relevant conditions? have some tact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T12:34:07-07:00","id":1443628,"title":"","content":"Malkavians having a tradition of valuing heterochromia as mark of a seer or something in selecting progeny makes the most sense. It's like asking why Kindred are so disproportionately physically young and pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:58:27-07:00","id":1443645,"title":"","content":"&quot;Any of these are far more interesting and less obnoxious than ' I got this eye when I became a member of The Crazy Bloodline'.&quot;<br /> I understand that mental conditions is very sensitive subject, but it is the part of the clan. Possibly, problems have started with transition from conception of triksterity and 'divine madness' to actual mental illness between editions.<br /> The topic was about already existing examples heterochromic malkavians, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","user":"trueann","date":". 04-14-2021, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:04:42-07:00","id":1443656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia?p=1443625#post1443625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah so like you're playing mage and suffering from paradox... rather than vampire.<br /> <br /> There's a few ways to get Heterochromia post embrace; Vicissitude, Chimestry, Arcane curse, Infernal pacts. Any of these are far more interesting and less obnoxious than ' I got this eye when I became a member of The Crazy Bloodline'. Imagine how that might feel to someone with any of the relevant conditions? have some tact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on; what makes 'a demon did this to me via infernal pact' any better morally than 'a mad vampire did this to me via its blood?' Seriously. What the heck. 'Have some tact?' C'mon.<br /> <br /> You also act like saying 'a demon did it' defacto represents a better story, somehow. Physical or supernatural flaws are both things vampires can have. Those flaws shouldn't just exist because you spent some points on them, they should be take with an in-universe explanation. I personally like the Dementation angle, but there are plenty of other strange things in the World of Darkness that may be responsible for the strange eyes of the Malkavians.<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe Malkav had heterochromia and just likes mirroring its own traits in its progeny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T22:18:18-07:00","id":1443704,"title":"","content":"Maybe we should use Occam's razor and use the simplest explanation: heterochromia is abnormal and that's what draw Malkavians to people with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T22:50:54-07:00","id":1443707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443001-malkavians-and-heterochromia?p=1443656#post1443656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hold on; what makes 'a demon did this to me via infernal pact' any better morally than 'a mad vampire did this to me via its blood?' Seriously. What the heck. 'Have some tact?' C'mon.<br /> <br /> You also act like saying 'a demon did it' defacto represents a better story, somehow. Physical or supernatural flaws are both things vampires can have. Those flaws shouldn't just exist because you spent some points on them, they should be take with an in-universe explanation. I personally like the Dementation angle, but there are plenty of other strange things in the World of Darkness that may be responsible for the strange eyes of the Malkavians.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Odin sold his eye for knowledge, it was a sacrifice, his eye didn't go missing when his mental faculties started to play up. What you're doing is both trivializing and glamourizing mental illnesses whilst doing the exact same thing towards deformities. It's like playing a fish malk but wanting to insult more people. It plays up that &quot;Flawed body=Flawed mind&quot; idea that some people have. It's just an ugly thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}